                     /note="Domain:cl17225:DAHP_synth_1 DAHP synthetase I
                     family. NeuB is the prokaryotic N-acetylneuraminic acid
                     (Neu5Ac) synthase. It catalyzes the direct formation of
                     Neu5Ac (the most common sialic acid) by condensation of
                     phosphoenolpyruvate (PEP) and N-acetylmannosamine (ManNAc).
                     This reaction has only been observed in prokaryotes;
                     eukaryotes synthesize the 9-phosphate form, Neu5Ac-9-P, and
                     utilize ManNAc-6-P instead of ManNAc. Such eukaryotic
                     enzymes are not present in this family. This family also
                     contains SpsE spore coat polysaccharide biosynthesis
                     proteins. [Superfamily, Aligned:13-344, Eval:4.9e-173,
                     score:482.1]"
                     /note="MGA_19"
