                     /note="WP_014207751.1 globin domain-containing protein
                     (Acinetobacter) [pid:94.9%, q_cov:100.0%, s_cov:100.0%,
                     Eval:6.7e-135]"
                     /note="Domain:cl21461:Globin_like Globin-like proteins.
                     This family includes protoglobin from Methanosarcina
                     acetivorans C2A. It is also found near the N-terminus of
                     the Haem-based aerotactic transducer HemAT in Bacillus
                     subtilis. It is part of the haemoglobin superfamily.
                     Protoglobin has specific loops and an amino-terminal
                     extension which leads to the burying of the haem within the
                     matrix of the protein. Protoglobin-specific apolar tunnels
                     allow the access of O2, CO and NO to the haem distal site.
                     In HemAT it acts as an oxygen sensor domain. [Superfamily,
                     Aligned:1-149, Eval:9.6e-58, score:178.3]"
                     /note="MGA_487"
