                     /note="Domain:cl21528:Lipocalin Lipocalin / cytosolic
                     fatty-acid binding protein family. ApoM is a 25 kDa plasma
                     protein associated with high-density lipoproteins (HDLs).
                     ApoM is important in the formation of pre-ss-HDL and also
                     in increasing cholesterol efflux from macrophage foam
                     cells. Lipoproteins consist of lipids solubilized by
                     apolipoproteins. ApoM lacks an external amphipathic motif
                     and is uniquely secreted to plasma without cleavage of its
                     terminal signal peptide. [Superfamily, Aligned:27-194,
                     Eval:5.0e-54, score:167.2]"
