                     /note="Domain:cl00768:CitG ATP:dephospho-CoA
                     triphosphoribosyl transferase. This protein acts in
                     cofactor biosynthesis, preparing the coenzyme A derivative
                     that becomes attached to the malonate decarboxylase acyl
                     carrier protein (or delta subunit). The closely related
                     protein CitG of citrate lyase produces the same molecule,
                     but the two families are nonetheless readily separated.
                     [Biosynthesis of cofactors, prosthetic groups, and
                     carriers, Other] [Superfamily, Aligned:9-288, Eval:2.9e-43,
                     score:146.8]"
