                     /locus_tag="LOCUS_10550"
                     /note="Domain:cl28567:HI1514 Phage tail tape-measure
                     protein, controls tail length   [Mobilome: prophages,
                     transposons]. Proteins containing this domain are strictly
                     bacterial, including bacteriophage and prophage regions of
                     bacterial genomes. Most members are 800 to 1800 amino acids
                     long, making them among the longest predicted proteins of
                     their respective phage genomes, where they are encoded in
                     tail protein regions. This roughly 80-residue domain
                     described here usually begins between residue 100 and 250.
                     Many members are known or predicted to act as phage tail
                     tape measure proteins, a minor tail component that
                     regulates tail length. [Superfamily, Aligned:314-404,
                     Eval:5.0e-08, score:53.3, N-term missing]"
                     /note="MGA_1058"
