     CDS             79816..80091
                     /product="type II toxin-antitoxin system Phd/YefM family
                     antitoxin"
                     /inference="COORDINATES:ab initio
                     prediction:MetaGeneAnnotator"
                     /inference="similar to AA sequence:RefSeq:WP_000213183.1"
                     /transl_table=11
                     /codon_start=1
                     /translation="MNHIIHSRFVASVSELKKNPTAVVQNAFGEAVAILNRNNPEFYCV
                     PAAMYERMMDLIEDQELIKLAEQVDTDETVKVSINELRARVLKNSS"
                     /locus_tag="LOCUS_10840"
                     /note="WP_000213183.1 type II toxin-antitoxin system
                     Phd/YefM family antitoxin (Vibrio) [pid:51.4%, q_cov:79.1%,
                     s_cov:87.8%, Eval:1.8e-15]"
                     /note="Domain:cl09153:PhdYeFM_antitox Antitoxin Phd_YefM,
                     type II toxin-antitoxin system. This model recognizes a
                     region of about 55 amino acids toward the N-terminal end of
                     bacterial proteins of about 85 amino acids in length. The
                     best-characterized member is prevent-host-death (phd) of
                     bacteriophage P1, the antidote partner of death-on-curing
                     (doc) (TIGR01550) in an addiction module. Addiction modules
                     prevent plasmid curing by killing the host cell as the
                     longer-lived killing protein persists while the gene for
                     the shorter-lived antidote is lost. Note, however, that
                     relatively few members of this family appear to be plasmid
                     or phage-encoded. Also, there is little overlap, except for
                     phage P1 itself, of species with this family and with the
                     doc family. [Cellular processes, Toxin production and
                     resistance, Mobile and extrachromosomal element functions,
                     Other] [Superfamily, Aligned:11-62, Eval:2.9e-08,
                     score:43.9, C-term missing]"
                     /note="MGA_1087"
