                     is involved in water permeability in the cuticles of fruit.
                     Mouse Tango2 has been found to be expressed during early
                     embryogenesis in mice. This protein contains a conserved
                     NRDE motif. This gene has been characterized in Drosophila
                     melanogaster and named as transport and Golgi organisation
                     2, hence the name Tango2. [Superfamily, Aligned:1-231,
                     Eval:6.9e-63, score:195.9]"
                     /note="MGA_1251"
