                     /note="Domain:cl26247:DNA_pol3_delta2 DNA polymerase III,
                     delta subunit. This model represents the well-conserved
                     first ~ 365 amino acids of the translation of the dnaX
                     gene. The full-length product of the dnaX gene in the model
                     bacterium E. coli is the DNA polymerase III tau subunit. A
                     translational frameshift leads to early termination and a
                     truncated protein subunit gamma, about 1/3 shorter than tau
                     and present in roughly equal amounts. This frameshift
                     mechanism is not necessarily universal for species with DNA
                     polymerase III but appears conserved in the exterme
                     thermophile Thermus thermophilis. [DNA metabolism, DNA
                     replication, recombination, and repair] [Superfamily,
                     Aligned:27-190, Eval:1.5e-24, score:100.9, C-term missing]"
