                     /note="frameshifted, insertion/deletion at around 23686"
                     /note="Domain:cl26457:T2SSJ Type II secretion system
                     (T2SS), protein J. This model represents GspJ, one of two
                     proteins highly conserved at their N-termini and described
                     by pfam02501 but easily separable phylogenetically. The
                     other is GspI. Both GspI and GspJ are proteins of the type
                     II secretion pathway, or main terminal branch of the
                     general secretion pathway. This pathway carries proteins
                     across the outer membrane. Note that proteins of type II
                     secretion are cryptic in E. coli K-12 - present but not yet
                     demonstrated to act on any target. [Superfamily,
                     Aligned:3-121, Eval:1.1e-08, score:50.1, C-term missing]"
                     /note="MGA_1656"
