                     /note="Domain:cl01067:Dyp_perox Dyp-type peroxidase family.
                     A defined member of this superfamily is Dyp, a
                     dye-decolorizing peroxidase that lacks a typical
                     heme-binding region. A distinct, uncharacterized branch
                     (TIGR01412) of this superfamily has a typical twin-arginine
                     dependent signal sequence characteristic of exported
                     proteins with bound redox cofactors. [Superfamily,
                     Aligned:1-310, Eval:1.2e-72, score:225.3]"
