                     /note="Domain:cl25429:PALP Pyridoxal-phosphate dependent
                     enzyme. This model represents threonine dehydratase, the
                     first step in the pathway converting threonine into
                     isoleucine. At least two other clades of biosynthetic
                     threonine dehydratases have been characterized by models
                     (TIGR01124 and TIGR01127). Those sequences described by
                     this model are exclusively found in species containg the
                     rest of the isoleucine pathway and which are generally
                     lacking in members of the those other two clades of
                     threonine dehydratases. Members of this clade are also
                     often gene clustered with other elements of the isoleucine
