                     /note="Domain:cl27678:AMP-binding AMP-binding enzyme.
                     Proteins in this family belong to the AMP-binding enzyme
                     family (pfam00501). Members activate 2,3-dihydroxybenzoate
                     (DHB) by ligation of AMP from ATP with the release of
                     pyrophosphate; many are involved in synthesis of
                     siderophores such as enterobactin, vibriobactin,
                     vulnibactin, etc. The most closely related proteine
                     believed to differ in function activates salicylate rather
                     than DHB. [Transport and binding proteins, Cations and iron
                     carrying compounds] [Superfamily, Aligned:1-540,
                     Eval:0.0e+00, score:813.6]"
