                     Eval:5.2e-55]"
                     /note="Domain:cl09190:MAPEG MAPEG family. This family is
                     has been called MAPEG (Membrane Associated Proteins in
                     Eicosanoid and Glutathione metabolism). It includes
                     proteins such as Prostaglandin E synthase. This enzyme
                     catalyzes the synthesis of PGE2 from PGH2 (produced by
                     cyclooxygenase from arachidonic acid). Because of
                     structural similarities in the active sites of FLAP, LTC4
                     synthase and PGE synthase, substrates for each enzyme can
                     compete with one another and modulate synthetic activity.
                     [Superfamily, Aligned:1-107, Eval:2.7e-26, score:91.7]"
                     /note="MGA_3291"
