                     /note="Domain:cl17173:AdoMet_MTases N/A. SAMBD is the
                     domain at the N-terminus of proteins arginine
                     methyltransferase 10 proteins. Protein arginine
                     methyltransferases catalyze the transfer of methyl groups
                     from S-adenosylmethionine - SAM - to arginine residues in
                     target proteins thereby releasing S-adensoylhomocystein -
                     SAH - as a product. Post-translational modification of
                     arginine plays important roles in the eukaryotic cell such
