                     /note="Domain:cl23863:BrnA_antitoxin BrnA antitoxin of type
                     II toxin-antitoxin system. CopG antitoxin is a member of a
                     type II toxin-antitoxin system family found in bacteria and
                     archaea. Most antitoxins encoded by the relBE and parDE
                     loci belong to the MetJ/Arc/CopG family of dimeric proteins
                     which bind DNA through N-terminal ribbon-helix-helix (RHH)
                     motifs. The toxin for CopG proteins falls into the family
                     BrnT_toxin, pfam04365. [Superfamily, Aligned:3-99,
                     Eval:3.6e-19, score:72.5]"
